I'd put all three pieces in one file, `routing.toml`. The payments override becomes a per-service field instead of code. I replayed September through both versions and every alert routes the same way. I haven't changed anything in the project.

```toml
# Severity decides the channel; service decides the team.
# `page_team`, when set, takes page-channel alerts instead of `team`.

[channels]
sev1 = "page"
sev2 = "page"
sev3 = "slack"
sev4 = "email"

[services]
checkout      = { team = "storefront" }
search        = { team = "discovery" }
catalog       = { team = "discovery" }
payments      = { team = "billing", page_team = "finance-oncall" }
ledger        = { team = "billing", page_team = "finance-oncall" }
notifications = { team = "platform" }
auth          = { team = "identity" }
inventory     = { team = "fulfilment" }
shipping      = { team = "fulfilment" }
```

`route.py` would shrink to a loader plus this. `FINANCE_SERVICES`, `URGENT` and `apply_payments_override` would go away:

```python
def route(service, severity):
    svc = ROUTING["services"][service]
    channel = ROUTING["channels"][severity]
    team = svc.get("page_team", svc["team"]) if channel == "page" else svc["team"]
    return team, channel
```

This stops the drift because "urgent" no longer has its own list. It now just means "the channel is page", and the finance exception sits on the same line as the owner. If someone moves payments to another team or adds a new money-path service, the exception is right in front of them. The one behaviour change to accept: if sev3 is ever switched to page, finance would take payments and ledger sev3 alerts too. Today the hard-coded `URGENT` set would silently miss that.

**Check against September:** all 812 alerts route identically under both versions, and so do all 36 service and severity combinations. The prototype and replay script are in `/tmp/routing_proposal/` (`routing.toml` and `replay.py`). The file uses `tomllib`, which needs Python 3.11 or later.

**A mismatch you should settle first:** the docstring says urgent money-path alerts page finance "as well as the owner", but the code replaces the owner. In September, 22 alerts (payments and ledger at sev1 or sev2) went only to `finance-oncall`, and billing got nothing. My proposal keeps the current replace behaviour. If "as well as" is what you meant, `route()` would have to return more than one team, and every caller would need to change. Which one do you want?
